## How it began

Provident began as a passion project, with a simple conviction: a coin that has survived decades, or millennia, deserves a holder and label worthy of it. Our first designs drew on classical and historical themes, and that idea still runs through everything we make, whether a label is meant for a casual collector, an enthusiast or a historian.

## How we work

Our graders are experienced numismatists. Every coin we accept is examined for authenticity, attributed, graded and reviewed before it is sealed, and every result is recorded under its own certificate number. Read the [full process](/process) and the [grading standards](/grading-standards) we apply.

## What we value

**Preservation.** A coin should pass to the next generation as it reached us, protected and unchanged.

**Excellence.** Rigorous standards, applied to every coin, whatever its value.

**Innovation.** Considered design, from the holder to the label, always in the service of the coin.

**Openness.** Every certificate on record, and open to anyone who holds the coin. [Verify a certificate](/verify).

## Where we are

We are based in Venice, Florida, and receive coins by mail from collectors and the trade. To discuss a coin or a submission, [contact us](/contact).
